## Hints for Future Agents
Edge and Chrome are not excluded by name anywhere. Any cask with auto_updates true is skipped by update.sh. Check a cask with `brew info --cask <name>`; the header shows "(auto_updates)" when covered. Ghostty is installed via brew on this machine but is NOT in essential-brew-overrides.sh's mac_cask_packages list. The note on d8a0390 claims Edge does not declare auto_updates; that was wrong and bfd1074 corrected the approach. `git commit` in this repo triggers an autosync hook that pushes master to origin immediately, so there is no window to amend. shellfmt.sh appears to stage the file it formats (the edit showed as staged before any `git add`).

## Codebase Discoveries
Ghostty's built-in updater is configurable via `auto-update = off|check|download` and `auto-update-channel = stable|tip` in the Ghostty config (macOS only). When unset, Sparkle's user defaults preference applies.

